Psalm 119:81-88

81 My sóul yéarns for your salvátion;
I hópe in your wórd.
82 My éyes yéarn to sée your prómise.
I ásk, ``Whén will you cómfort me?"

83 I am like a wíneskin shríveled by smóke,
yet I remémber your státutes.
84 How lóng must your sérvant endúre?
When will you bríng júdgment on my fóes?

85 For mé the próud have dúg pítfalls;
they defý your láw.
86 Your commánds are all trúe; then hélp me
when líes oppréss me.

87 They have álmost máde an énd of me on éarth,
yet I forsáke not your précepts.
88 In your mérciful lóve, give me lífe;
I will obéy the decrées of your líps.

Glóry to the Fáther, and to the Són,
and to the Hóly Spírit:
as it wás in the begínning, is nów,
and will be for éver. Amén.
